 times over), `colors` (else one picked for each piece). More models: note, notes (a pair), petal, curl (uploaded), ball, cube, bar, strip (plain shapes), square (a flat square). More looks: fire (its own light, never shaded: flames and embers), paper (crisp folds), bright (a lit block), glass (a see-through goo bubble). More moves: `upright` (stands up, turning like a sign), `align: grid` (square to the plane as it was when the piece left, long side mostly along the path), `jump` (studs: snaps sideways 8 times a second), `level` (flies nose-first along the path, right way up), `axes` (a grid piece's long side: how often along the path, across it, up), `lattice` (studs: pieces start on a grid this wide, so they line up), `run` (studs a second: races back along the path). Also models dart (a tiny paper plane) and jog (a bent circuit trace), both uploaded, and chip (a plain block). In the game (src/client/PlaneTrails.luau): soft, spark and square pieces are Roblox particles using Roblox's own smoke, sparkle and square pictures; flake, strip, cube, bar and ball are plain shapes made there; the others are the uploaded models in `meshes` (tools/art/trail_pieces.py makes them; uploaded 2026-11-16 as Models, records in assets/models/trails/upload-<piece>.json; these are their inner mesh ids; 0 = not uploaded yet, so that piece is not drawn).",
